- Story & Context: Crouched behind a barricade of blown tube amplifiers inside an abandoned municipal pump house, Vane "Crank" Hallowell wiped black valve grease from his cheeks while the bitter taste of bootleg corn-gin scorched his tongue. He had just discovered that diverting tidal power to the pirate radio tower had inadvertently flooded his own brother’s squatter bunk three levels below the sea-line. Weeping between hyper-syncopated drum-machine fills and screeching banjo slides, Vane screamed into the crackling PA, "I traded our dry bed for sixty seconds of goddamn rhythm!" before lodging a pearl-handled pocketknife straight into his own wedge monitor. The rooftop crowd did not offer sympathy; they screamed the swinging refrains back into his face until the surge tank overflowed onto their ankles.
